course: dictionary
lesson: 10298
title: Touchy words and touchy subjects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Touchy has two meanings. A touchy person gets upset or annoyed very easily, so you need to be careful what you say to them. A touchy subject is one that can upset people, so it needs to be talked about carefully.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «Families sometimes argue over who gets what after a death, especially a house, because grief makes people touchy and old quarrels come back.» Grief is the deep sadness after someone dies, so touchy here means people get upset very easily.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. "Grief makes people easily upset" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Touchy is an adjective, so it can change to touchier and touchiest.
fact: «Touchy» means easily upset or annoyed.
fact: A touchy subject is one that needs careful talking because it may upset people, such as money, religion or someone's weight.
fact: Touchy can also mean sensitive: «She is touchy about her height.»
fact: Touchy-feely is informal and means showing your feelings a lot.
fact: Touchier means more touchy, and touchiest means the most touchy.
exercise: «Families sometimes argue over who gets what after a death, because grief makes people touchy.» What does touchy mean here? | Very happy and calm | *Easily upset or annoyed | Good at sports | Very quiet and shy
exercise: Sam says, «Don't ask Dad about his age, it's a touchy subject.» What does touchy subject mean? | A subject about touching things | A subject that is easy to learn | A subject with lots of pictures | *A subject that needs careful talking because it can upset people
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Families sometimes argue over who gets what after a death, because grief makes people touchy.» that describes people who get upset easily. | grief | argue | *touchy | death
test: Which word means showing your feelings a lot? | Quarrel | Touchier | Touchiest | *Touchy-feely
test: Which sentence uses touchy to mean that a subject could upset people? | *Money can be a touchy subject at home. | The dog ran across the park. | Mum baked a big chocolate cake. | We walked to school this morning.
exam: In «grief makes people touchy», which word could replace touchy and still make sense? | very tall | very fast | *easily upset | very tidy
